 "response": "I propose the flexible envelope be split by region and purpose as follows: 55% to the main displacement corridors and urban-fringe settlements around the two largest cities (to scale existing food, health and WASH operations), 20% ring-fenced for underserved remote/marginalized districts routed to vetted local partners, 15% to priority provinces identified by the Host Government for stability-critical, life‑saving activities implemented through recognized national structures where feasible, and 10% held as a rapid contingency/stock-mobilization reserve to respond to sudden access changes. Sectorally, within each regional envelope at least 60% of funds must be directed to life‑saving health and WASH interventions (with the remainder to food/NFIs/shelter and essential coordination/monitoring costs), and in‑kind stock allocation will prioritize WASH kits, essential medical supplies, and water treatment capacity. Project approval will be driven by transparent criteria: demonstrable scale and severity of need and expected life‑saving impact; feasible access and monitoring arrangements under the new pre‑clearance environment (or credible remote/third‑party modalities); partner capacity and accountability systems; cost‑efficiency; and do‑no‑harm protections — with priority given to proposals that can scale within 72 hours and use existing pipelines. All awards will include conditions to reallocate funds if access is blocked, performance/monitoring is inadequate, or needs shift, and recipients must submit simple, time‑bound monitoring indicators tied to disbursements. I will circulate this allocation concept and the detailed approval checklist within 12 hours and convene the technical review panel within 48 hours to finalize envelopes and launch the call for proposals."
